% Unification must respect arity: the `q(X, Y)` in the rule body should
% match the fact `q(1, 2)`, but not the shorter fact `q(1)`. Previously
% `q(X, Y)` unified with `q(1)`, binding only `X` and adding the
% non-ground fact `p(1, Y)` to the knowledge base.

q(1).
q(1, 2).

p(X, Y) <- q(X, Y).

? p(A, B).
